The MIT license above covers the code in this repository: fetch_data.py,
build.py, src/template.html, assets/styles.css and assets/app.js.

It does not cover the catalogue itself. The records in data/raw/,
data/viruses.json and data/meta.json are derived from:

  Zhang F, Lu L, Brierley L, Hietanen H, Woolhouse MEJ.
  Human-infective RNA virus database [dataset]. figshare; version 2, 2026.
  doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.30094726.v2
  Licensed CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

That license permits redistribution and adaptation with attribution, which is
why the workbook is committed here unchanged and why the citation appears on
every page of the site, in data/source.json and in DATA.md. Anyone reusing the
catalogue should cite Zhang et al. rather than this repository.

The risk scores in data/spillover.json are published by the SpillOver: Viral
Risk Ranking project (spillover.global). Credit for that ranking belongs to the
SpillOver team.
